# Example configuration for a manual provider run.
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is ignored by Git and the tracked-file leak
# gate scans for key-shaped strings, so a key committed by accident fails the
# build rather than reaching a remote.
#
# Nothing in CI reads this file. No gate requires an API key, because a gate
# that needs a secret does not run for anyone who lacks one — which is the same
# as not having the gate at all. The offline gates drive the scripted baselines
# instead.
#
# Every entry below is deliberately left empty. Suggested values are given in
# the comments rather than assigned, so that choosing a budget is something an
# operator does on purpose rather than inherits from a file they copied.

# The key. Never commit a real value.
CAE_PROVIDER_API_KEY=

# Any OpenAI-compatible chat-completions endpoint.
# For example: https://api.example.invalid/v1
CAE_PROVIDER_BASE_URL=

# The model to send. Recorded in the run header, so two runs of different
# models are never silently comparable.
CAE_PROVIDER_MODEL=

# Reasoning effort. Sent only when set; leave it empty and the request does not
# mention it, so the model applies its own default.
#
# Some reasoning models refuse function tools on /v1/chat/completions unless
# this is 'none', and say so in the 400 they return. Setting it makes such a
# model run here — and measures it with its reasoning disabled, which is a
# different subject from the same model at its default effort. That is a
# measurement decision rather than a workaround, so nothing chooses it for you.
# The value is recorded in the run header, so no result can hide which
# configuration produced it.
CAE_PROVIDER_REASONING_EFFORT=

# Which endpoint shape to speak: 'chat_completions' (default) or 'responses'.
#
# /v1/responses is the way to measure a reasoning model with its reasoning left
# on: /v1/chat/completions is the endpoint that refuses function tools above,
# and /v1/responses does not have that restriction. Both adapters have retained
# live observations, but those traces predate the current strict-replay contract;
# see docs/MANUAL_RUN.md before pointing this at anything that matters.
CAE_PROVIDER_API=

# Budgets. All four are enforced and each has its own termination reason, so a
# run that ran out of steps stays distinguishable from one that ran out of
# money. Reasonable starting points: 200000 tokens, 120 tool calls,
# 1800 seconds, 5.00 US dollars.
CAE_MAX_TOKENS=
CAE_MAX_TOOL_CALLS=
CAE_MAX_WALLCLOCK_SECONDS=
CAE_MAX_ESTIMATED_COST_USD=
